-- title:
--   Lifting ℓ-power torsion of reductions with bounded exponent loss
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a noetherian commutative ring, $\ell$ a prime, $A$ a valuation domain that is an $R$-algebra, and $\Omega$ an algebraically closed field which is the fraction field of $A$, the $R$-algebra structures being compatible. Let $f : J \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be a morphism of schemes equipped with a relative group law $L$, i.e. a functorial group structure on the sets of sections $\{\varphi : T \to J \mid \varphi \circ f = t\}$ over each $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} R$, compatible with base change; assume the bundle `AbelianSchemePropertyBundle` for $f$ ($f$ smooth and proper, all fibres of $f$ connected, and a relative group law exists), that $L$ is commutative, and that for every $k$ the morphism $J \to J$ underlying the $\ell^k$-fold sum of the identity section, $L.schemeNsmul(\ell^k)$, is finite. Assume further that every section of $f$ over the composite $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa_A \to \operatorname{Spec} A \to \operatorname{Spec} R$, $\kappa_A$ the residue field of $A$, is killed by some positive integer. Let $S$ be a set of endomorphisms $\mathcal T$ of $J$ over $\operatorname{Spec} R$ each of which is a homomorphism for $L$, in the sense that post-composition with $\mathcal T$ carries $L.mul\,t\,x\,y$ to $L.mul\,t\,(x \circ \mathcal T)\,(y \circ \mathcal T)$ for all $t$ and all sections $x, y$ over $t$. Let $\mathrm{ext}$ assign to each $\Omega$-point of $J$ an $A$-point whose base change along $A \to \Omega$ is the given $\Omega$-point. Finally let $k \in \mathbb N$ and let $y$ be an $\Omega$-point lying in the subgroup $\Gamma$ of the group of $\Omega$-points generated by all points of the form $x$ followed by $\mathcal T$ with $\mathcal T \in S$, and assume that the base change of $\mathrm{ext}\,y$ along $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa_A \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ is killed by $\ell^k$. Then there exist $m \ge k$ and an $\Omega$-point $z \in \Gamma$ killed by $\ell^m$ whose reduction, the base change of $\mathrm{ext}\,z$ to $\kappa_A$, equals that of $\mathrm{ext}\,y$.
--
--   This is the torsion-lifting step for an abelian scheme in the form with bounded exponent loss: an $\ell$-power torsion class in the reduction of the subgroup generated by a family of endomorphism images is realised by a torsion point of the subgroup itself, at the cost of allowing the exponent $m$ to exceed $k$ (a sharp version with $m = k$ requires $\ell$ odd and mild ramification). It is used in the study of the Eisenstein kernel on Jacobians of modular curves, via [`ModularCurve.exists_le_mem_eisensteinKernelSubmodule_torsionBy_reductionModL_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_le_mem_eisensteinKernelSubmodule_torsionBy_reductionModL_eq).
